    "A": "Own portable kernel and data locality. Retain 4f50d6458ecf4ccb as the scalar blocking reference; larger unrolling is low priority given its modest gain. Investigate position-only x/y/z scratch arrays to avoid reading interleaved velocities: initialize once and refresh during position integration, after the force barrier. Preserve coordinate bits and binary Body I/O, provide allocation-failure fallback, and measure total runtime including scratch maintenance. Deliver independently usable kernel/layout changes.",
    "B": "Own exact ARM64 SIMD. Lead with four-target candidate a486b82f661047f0, not the slower eight-target variant. Expose a block kernel usable inside C's worksharing loop without creating another parallel team. Keep one target per lane, ascending j accumulation, original expression grouping, and double sqrt/division followed by float conversion. Retain feature guards and complete scalar remainder/fallback paths. Do not introduce approximate reciprocal square roots, sqrtf substitution, or source-axis reductions.",
    "C": "Own parallel orchestration. Preserve f85d6cd3609f4fe9's persistent team, static target ownership, and force/position barriers as the leading design. Support scheduling complete SIMD target blocks with every remainder target owned exactly once. Investigate a general small-workload serial cutoff without assuming the other candidate's 128-body cutoff is optimal. Keep b60a0e38fe67496d's double-buffered, one-barrier scheme as an alternative for integration with faster kernels; never fuse position writes into a loop still reading the same position array.",
    "G": "Use f85d6cd3609f4fe9 as the measured incumbent. First integrate B's four-target NEON kernel into C's persistent-team, two-phase structure, preserving both barriers and unique tail ownership. Next compare the SIMD kernel with C's double-buffered scheme; its standalone loss need not predict its integrated result. Evaluate A's locality changes separately before stacking them. Keep eight-target SIMD and scalar-blocking hybrids lower priority. Validate and measure each complete program through the unchanged automatic pipeline, including allocation and I/O costs. Retain the fastest admissible measured program, even if every integration loses; do not multiply standalone speedups or merge all transformations unconditionally.",
    "analysis": "Focus exclusively on Problem C's ten-step all-pairs N-body simulation. Baseline is 0.658929 s. Persistent OpenMP candidate f85d6cd3609f4fe9 leads at 0.170245 s, about 3.87x faster; double buffering measured 0.173766 s. Four-target NEON measured 0.323776 s versus eight-target NEON's 0.335023 s. Scalar four-target blocking measured 0.597571 s versus pairing's 0.612579 s. Thus persistent OpenMP plus four-target NEON is the strongest unmeasured synthesis hypothesis, not an established additive gain. All roles must preserve per-target accumulation order, arithmetic precision and rounding behavior, synchronous timesteps, and the input count header/output-only Body payload format. Preserve correctness for every valid input, not merely the four checked cases. Keep compiler, oracle, tests, target, permissions, and budgets unchanged."
